MATCH: HttpTestingController|TestBed|expectOne|provideHttpClientTesting|NullInjectorError.*Http|Expected one matching request
---
Le spec Angular avec client HTTP de test rate presque toujours sur la CONFIG, pas sur la
logique. Gabarit qui passe (Angular moderne, standalone):

  import { TestBed } from '@angular/core/testing';
  import { provideHttpClient } from '@angular/common/http';
  import { provideHttpClientTesting, HttpTestingController } from '@angular/common/http/testing';

  describe('MonService', () => {
    let httpMock: HttpTestingController;
    beforeEach(() => {
      TestBed.configureTestingModule({
        providers: [provideHttpClient(), provideHttpClientTesting()],
      });
      httpMock = TestBed.inject(HttpTestingController);
    });
    afterEach(() => httpMock.verify());
    it('charge les donnees', () => {
      const svc = TestBed.inject(MonService);
      let out: unknown;
      svc.charger().subscribe(v => (out = v));
      httpMock.expectOne('/api/mon-endpoint').flush([{ id: 1 }]);
      expect(out).toBeTruthy();
    });
  });

Regles: provideHttpClient AVANT provideHttpClientTesting; expectOne doit matcher l'URL
EXACTE appelee par le service (params compris: sinon utiliser un predicat req =>
req.url.startsWith(...)); flush APRES subscribe; un composant standalone se teste via
TestBed.configureTestingModule({ imports: [MonComposant], providers: [...] }).
